54 665 Td
(PART 2: FACTUAL BASIS) Tj
T*
(1. The Plaintiff and the Corporate Defendant entered into a written Joint Venture Development Agreement) Tj
T*
(   dated January 15, 2025, governing the construction of a 28-storey tower at 1200 Burrard Street, Vancouver.) Tj
T*
(2. Pursuant to Clause 4.2 of the Agreement, the Corporate Defendant was appointed Managing Partner and was) Tj
T*
(   under strict contractual and fiduciary obligations to maintain transparent, unredacted accounting books.) Tj
T*
(3. On May 10, 2026, the Plaintiff contributed $1,500,000 into the project contingency account pursuant to a) Tj
T*
(   cash-call notice issued by the Individual Defendant, John Doe.) Tj
T*
(4. On August 12, 2026, the Corporate Defendant delivered its initial List of Documents, which listed high-level) Tj
T*
(   summary spreadsheets but entirely omitted underlying bank statements and general ledgers.) Tj
T*
(5. On September 14, 2026, counsel for the Plaintiff delivered a formal deficiency letter demanding production.) Tj
T*
(6. By letter dated September 28, 2026, the Defendants refused production, alleging 'commercial sensitivity'.) Tj
T*
(7. The documents sought are directly material to paragraphs 14 through 22 of the Notice of Civil Claim, wherein) Tj
T*
(   the Plaintiff pleads breach of contract, unauthorized redirection of contingency funds, and breach of duty.) Tj
T*
(8. The requested production is proportionate under Rule 1-3, having regard to the $1,500,000 at stake and the) Tj
T*
(   fact that electronic bank records can be produced in PDF format with minimal expense.) Tj
ET
endstream
